# Wave W17-S (Route 127 Trench): kelp floor — golden sand swim-path: a saturated golden trench sand carrying the lit patches in the floor\u2019s own art — bright pale-gold glints standing in two loose runs across the tread, the ways back up drawn as light on the path itself (design: lit sand patches marking the way back up, the surface keeping all its doors open over the forest). Route 127 Trench\u2019s own floor — the golden floor of the unmapped country: more saturated and more warmly lit than Route 124 Trench\u2019s pale daylight shaft sand, and golden where Route 128 Trench\u2019s breath floor is ember-flecked dusk.
